      "writtenOn": "2024-01-10T15:04:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`SkFontMgr::RefDefault` was a kind of magic global thing inside Skia-the-library. It forced knowing which SkFontMgr implementations were available at build time (when we want those implementations to be in separate non-registering shared objects). `TestFontMgr` is not in Skia-the-library but instead is application code. The application knows which parts of Skia it is going to have available so can depend on those SkFontMgr implementations existing at run time.",
      "parentUuid": "6570be3a_5ea07cfa",
      "revId": "18fe531054edb090dfb2c9a0fb258ad48c40dc17",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
